{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim formed the human.</b> Since He wanted to write 'and He placed there the human whom He had formed,' He mentioned here a second time the forming of the human. And the passages 'and He planted,' 'and it grew' — they were written to recall the commandment of the tree of knowledge." "<b>And He breathed into his nostrils the breath of life.</b> By His breathing — which is the holy spirit, something He did not breathe into the nostrils of any other creature. And why all this? So as to direct his mind to solve a riddle: that he would call the creatures their own names, which HaKadosh Barukh Hu had called them. And thus it is written: 'and whatsoever he would call it' — that is its name; meaning, it is the name that HaKadosh Barukh Hu had called it before He brought them to him." "<b>Breath of life.</b> A soul that lives forever and does not die at the death of the body."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:25.582775238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}